# Party banter in Krezk and at the Abbey of St. Markovia. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only
# while its condition holds. Party members speak through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_wall
if visited:krezk and not flag.krezk_gate_open and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: A wall that big, and they still look at every face on the road. Fair enough. I'd look at us twice.
interject tag:cheerful: We have very trustworthy faces.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Mine's very honest. It's the horns that let it down. Do you think they'd take an apricot?
endif
-> END

~ banter_angel
if flag.abbot_nature_known and not flag.abbot_fate and name:kip_smudgewick and name:ratatoille
interject name:kip_smudgewick: A real angel, sewing dead girls together. I always thought if I met one, I'd ask for help with a paperwork matter.
interject name:ratatoille: The treatises say they are made for one purpose. Leave one too long without it, and it finds another.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Not yet, please. Let me pray before anyone explains him to me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_belviews
if flag.belview_family_met
interject tag:curious: The Belviews repeat everything you say. Everything. I said "hello" and got it back in my own voice from six directions.
interject tag:blunt: They were a family from Krezk. Farmers. He did that to them and called it a gift.
interject tag:pious: Then we treat them like a family from Krezk. Whatever they look like now.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bride
if flag.abbot_bride_revealed and not flag.abbot_fate and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:thistle: A wife, stitched out of dead girls, to make him gentle. Grandda tried that with a mean dog. Got it a friend.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: And?
interject name:thistle: Dog ate the friend.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Then nobody's giving him a friend. Not her. Not anyone.
endif
-> END

~ banter_dress
if flag.wedding_dress_found and not flag.wedding_dress_delivered
interject tag:loyal: Anna's dress. She folded it in lavender. We're carrying it up a mountain to put it on a dead girl.
if tag:loyal
interject class:cleric: For her son. She knew what she was doing. That's what makes it hard to carry.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_letter
if flag.markovia_letter_read and not flag.abbot_fate
interject tag:scholarly: "Patience is how he feeds." The saint saw through him four hundred years ago. In one line.
interject tag:blunt: And the angel kept the letter under a floorboard.
interject tag:scholarly: No. The angel lost it. Clovin kept it. That's the part I keep thinking about.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pool
if flag.ireena_pool_vision and guest:ireena and (tag:curious or name:liriel_dawnsong)
if tag:curious
interject tag:curious: Ireena. The man in the water. Do you want to talk about it?
else
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Ireena. The man in the water. Would you like to speak of him?
endif
interject guest:ireena: No. Yes. Later. Ask me again when we're somewhere with a fire and no water anywhere.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hunter
if guest:ezmerelda and name:ratatoille and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:ratatoille: Mademoiselle, is it true Van Richten writes his notes in three ciphers? I have a theory about the third.
interject guest:ezmerelda: Four. The fourth is his handwriting.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Oh, I like her.
interject guest:ezmerelda: Everyone does, at first. Ask Rudolph.
endif
-> END

~ banter_wedding
if flag.abbot_fate == "wedding" and name:kip_smudgewick and class:cleric
interject class:cleric: We let it happen. A bride in a cart, waving at nobody.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: We got the boy healed. That was the bargain. I've made worse ones, and I still sleep. Mostly.
interject class:cleric: I haven't. I suppose I'll learn. I would rather not.
endif
-> END

~ banter_repentant
if flag.abbot_fate == "repentant"
interject tag:pious: He walked up the mountain to be judged. I keep wondering who's going to do it.
interject tag:curious: Maybe nobody. Maybe that's the point. You go anyway.
endif
-> END

~ banter_slain
if flag.abbot_fate == "slain" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:wren_featherfoot: No blood. Just light, and then nothing. What was that, that we killed?
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Something that forgot what it was for. Sir Pellam prayed for everything he ever had to kill. I'll pray for this one.
endif
-> END

~ banter_cells
if flag.wards_cells_fought
interject tag:cheerful: Those weren't monsters. They were people he'd been practising on.
interject tag:blunt: They were both. That's the worst thing about this valley. Everything's both.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ilya
if flag.ilya_fate == "healed"
interject tag:cheerful: Did you see the boy? Shouting his own name down the well. I want to do that.
interject tag:blunt: Do it, then.
interject tag:cheerful: Not with everyone watching!
endif
-> END
